feat(cpu): an Apple Silicon processor gets its CPU device

On an Apple Silicon Mac under Linux the CPU repository fails to start
with "cpuinfo either not found or missing data on this system!", an
error on every daemon start. arm64 cpuinfo carries no model name and no
physical id, and the Raspberry Pi fallback reads a Model line Apple
Silicon does not print either. Even named, no CPU device would be built,
because devices are only built on a CPU temperature driver, and an
Apple Silicon Mac has none: its die temperatures come through the SMC.
Its frequencies are missing too, since cpuinfo prints no cpu MHz.

When the device tree marks the machine apple,arm-platform, the board's
device tree model names the processor, the same fallback the Raspberry
Pi gets from its Model line, and one CPU device is built from load and
frequency alone. The frequencies are each core's cpuinfo_cur_freq, the
clock the cluster actually runs at, read by the daemon as root. Nothing
changes on any machine whose device tree does not say apple.

Measured on a J316c MacBook Pro (M1 Max), kernel 7.1.13. The cpuinfo
fixture is that machine's own.

